===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person with a choleric [[temperament]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1915|author=[[w:John Adams (educationist)|John Adams]]|title=Making the Most of One’s Mind|location=New York|publisher=Hodder & Stoughton|page=21|url=https://catalog.hathitrust.org/Record/001279888
|passage=The '''cholerics''' show ambition, stubbornness, love of work, courage {{...}}}}
#* '''1984''', {{w|Tim LaHaye}}, ''Your Temperament: Discover its Potential'', republished as ''Why You Act the Way You Do'', Carol Stream, Illinois: Tyndale House, 2012,<sup>[https://books.google.ca/books?id=Y8vT2G-gDZUC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false]</sup>
#*: No one utters more caustic comments than a sarcastic '''choleric'''!
# A person [[suffer]]ing from [[cholera]] (infectious disease).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1832|author=w:Ashbel Smith|title=The Cholera Spasmodica|location=New York|publisher=P. Hill|page=59|url=https://catalog.hathitrust.org/Record/100139563
|passage=Persons laboring under pulmonary affections appear to be less liable than others, though I have found softened tubercles in some '''cholerics'''.}}

